Cell["\<\
Population is highly correlated to number of new build and consumer \
electricity price. I am keeping number of new build and discarding population.
New build and consumer electricity price are highly correlated but to start \
with I am keeping both variables.
Bid price is not correlated with demand or with any other variables. \
Discarding for now.
Gas demand is not correlated with demand or with any other variables. \
Discarding for now.
Average temperature is quite highly correlated with percentage renewable. The \
cofounding variable is time, due to global warming the average temperature in \
the UK is going up and over time more wind and solar farms have been \
installed throughout the UK.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.929683229805376*^9, 3.929683276877846*^9}, {
  3.9296833373590984`*^9, 3.929683481912271*^9}, {3.929683528560971*^9, 
  3.929683601342964*^9}, {3.929683658724428*^9, 3.9296836641454983`*^9}, {
  3.9296838005914955`*^9, 
  3.929683847830353*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0417c22c-ea38-bc47-a18a-\
9abae0d86682"],

